## 7. CSS & Styling Patterns

### 7.1 Global Design Tokens

`packages/ui-kit/src/styles/base.css` defines `:root` CSS custom properties (colors, fonts, spacing, border-radius). Every app gets these tokens because `ui-kit/src/index.js` imports `base.css` at the top.

### 7.2 CSS Modules

Every component's styles are in `.module.css` files. In test configs, `generateScopedName` is set to `"[local]"` so test selectors can use the raw class names. In production, the hash-based naming is used.

### 7.3 Global Reset

`apps/host/styles.css` contains minimal global resets (`overflow: hidden`, `margin: 0`, `background-color: #ffffff`, and `--sidebar-margin` CSS variable).

### 7.4 LucideProvider

`mf-causes` wraps its tree in `<LucideProvider size={16} strokeWidth={1.75}>` so all `lucide-react` icons share consistent sizing. Icons in `ui-kit` are custom inline SVG components in `packages/ui-kit/src/Icons/Icons.jsx` (not from Lucide).

---

## 8. i18n Pattern

- Each micro frontend has its **own i18next instance** (via `i18next.createInstance()`), initialized with `initReactI18next`.
- Translation files live at `src/locales/en/text.json` inside each app.
- Only English (`en`) exists today, but the structure allows adding `locales/<lang>/text.json` files.
- The host and each MF import and use their own instance, passed explicitly to `useTranslation(undefined, { i18n })`.

