## 12. Real File Content Examples

### Example: Host Main Entry (`apps/host/src/main.jsx`)

- Imports `react`, `react-dom/client`, `react-router-dom`
- Imports `@albert-fe/ui-kit` (triggers `base.css` injection)
- Imports `./i18n`
- Imports `App`, `AuthProvider`, `PermissionsProvider`
- Mounts React root into `#root` with `BrowserRouter` wrapping both providers

### Example: MF Causes Exposed Component (`apps/mf-causes/src/Component.jsx`)

- Imports `react`, `react-i18next`
- Imports from `@albert-fe/ui-kit` (`Card`, `Tag`)
- Imports local components (`CaseDashboardComponent`)
- Wraps everything in `<LucideProvider>` and `<ToastProvider>`
- Exports `Component` as the default entry for Module Federation

### Example: UI Kit Barrel (`packages/ui-kit/src/index.js`)

- First line: `import "./styles/base.css"` (injects tokens)
- Then re-exports every component in named and default forms:
  - `export { TextBox, default as TextBoxDefault } from "./TextBox/TextBox"`
  - `export { Button, default as ButtonDefault } from "./Button/Button"`
  - And so on for all 15+ components

### Example: API Client Barrel (`packages/api-client/src/index.js`)

- Re-exports `ApiService`, `PermissionsService`, `CasesService`
- Re-exports all Keycloak functions: `initKeycloak`, `getKeycloak`, `isAuthenticated`, `getToken`, `getUserProfile`, `login`, `logout`, `updateToken`, `saveTokensToSession`, `clearSessionTokens`, `saveUserToSession`, `SESSION_KEYS`
- Re-exports `seedDevSession`, `HttpClient`, `ApiError`, `authInterceptor`

### Example: `utils/environmentVariables.js`

- A single helper function `getEnvironmentVariable(variableName)`
- Checks `window.__ENV__` first (for Docker runtime injection)
- Falls back to `import.meta.env[variableName]` (for Vite dev/build)
- Returns `null` if not found

---

## 13. Security & Environment Variable Handling

- Environment variables must be prefixed with `VITE_` to be accessible in the browser via `import.meta.env`.
- A shared `getEnvironmentVariable()` utility in `utils/environmentVariables.js` also checks `window.__ENV__`, which is populated at runtime by `inject-env.js` for dynamic Docker deployments.
- `keycloakService.js` reads Keycloak config (`URL`, `Realm`, `ClientID`) through this helper and throws if any are missing.